---
import './figures.css';
---
<figure class="cl-figure" data-table-route aria-labelledby="table-route-title">
  <figcaption id="table-route-title"><span class="cl-number">Figure 1</span> The gateway and the table’s home</figcaption>
  <div class="cl-panel">
    <div class="cl-controls"><label>SQL gateway <select data-gateway aria-label="SQL gateway"><option>North</option><option>West</option></select></label></div>
    <div class="cl-card cl-active"><b data-origin data-live>North · SQL gateway</b><span>SELECT price FROM products WHERE product_id = 'P7'</span></div>
    <div class="cl-arrow" data-route data-live>↓ KV work crosses North → West</div>
    <div class="cl-three">
      <div class="cl-region"><strong>North</strong><span class="cl-small">Database primary region</span><div class="cl-card"><b>Other replica</b><span class="cl-small">A copy is not ordinary current-read authority.</span></div></div>
      <div class="cl-region cl-active"><strong>West · table home</strong><div class="cl-card" data-owner><b>Leaseholder</b><span>P7 · price 20.00</span><span>Stock 0 after purchase 103</span></div></div>
      <div class="cl-region"><strong>East</strong><div class="cl-card"><b>Other replica</b><span class="cl-small">Replica roles depend on the survival goal.</span></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="cl-arrow" data-return data-live>Result has not returned</div>
    <p class="cl-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The application connects to North. Products is homed in West; the database’s primary region does not override that choice.</p>
    <div class="cl-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 1 playback"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span class="cl-step" data-step>1 / 3</span></div><div class="cl-hold" data-hold><span></span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="cl-caption">A model of an established, healthy placement with ordinary current reads and usable routing. One leaseholder box stands for the relevant product range. Other ranges, protocol messages and replica counts are omitted; no regional timing is implied.</p>
  <details><summary>Both routes as text</summary><p>Through North: SQL gateway North → relevant product-range leaseholder West → price 20.00 returns to North. Through West: the gateway and leaseholder are in the same region. Both return the same price. A nearby replica in North does not by itself authorise an ordinary current read there.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll('[data-table-route]').forEach(root => {
  const choice = root.querySelector('[data-gateway]') as HTMLSelectElement;
  const player = stepper(root,{steps:()=>3,draw:step=>{
    const local=choice.value==='West';
    root.querySelector('[data-origin]').textContent=`${choice.value} · SQL gateway`;
    root.querySelector('[data-route]').textContent=step===0?'↓ Find the relevant product range':local?'↓ KV work stays within West':'↓ KV work crosses North → West';
    root.querySelector('[data-owner]').classList.toggle('cl-active',step>=1);
    root.querySelector('[data-return]').textContent=step<2?'Result has not returned':local?'↑ Price 20.00 · returned within West':'↑ Price 20.00 · West → North';
    root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=[`The application connects to ${choice.value}. Products is homed in West; the database’s primary region does not override that choice.`,local?'The gateway reaches the product-range leaseholder within West. Same region does not necessarily mean the same node.':'The gateway reaches the product-range leaseholder in West. North’s other copy does not make this ordinary current read local.',`The application receives 20.00. ${local?'This route avoids a regional gateway-to-owner trip.':'The result crosses back to North.'} The stored price and stock are unchanged.`][step];
  }});
  choice.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
});
</script>
